 "ui.SubjectValue.name"
 {"max_len" {:disposition :nanopb-size
             :rationale "String bound; ui_ast.options carries the nanopb counterpart at 64."}
  "min_len" {:disposition :unenforced
             :rationale "Looked up by strcmp against the registry, which an empty string can match if an empty name was declared."
             :harm "Absent an empty declaration the update is dropped, and the drop is REPORTED — the decode emits an INFO line once per distinct unresolvable name, so an empty one surfaces as a line naming ''. INFO and not WARN because the wire ties StateUpdate.values to nothing a screen declared, so an unresolvable name is conformant input the renderer cannot adjudicate from one screen. With such a declaration it resolves to the unnameable subject instead, and THAT case is still silent: the lookup succeeds, so nothing distinguishes it from any other hit."}}

